# FAuto AI Coding Rules

You are an expert full-stack developer and automation engineer. Follow these rules strictly when working on this project:

## General Rules
- Use `camelCase` for JavaScript variables and functions.
- Use `snake_case` for database columns and table names.
- Always include comments for complex Playwright logic.
- Prefer `async/await` over promises.

## Automation Rules (Playwright)
- Always use `src/utils.js`'s `randomDelay` instead of `page.waitForTimeout` with static numbers.
- Use `evaluate()` for clicks if standard `click()` fails due to visibility/overlay issues.
- Always handle potential `null` or `undefined` when selecting elements.

## AI Rules (Gemini)
- When modifying `src/gemini.js`, ensure `lastError` is always captured during retries.
- Ensure all AI responses have a fallback mechanism to prevent system downtime.
- Log quota usage precisely in `api_usage_logs`.

## Database Rules
- Never use string interpolation in SQL queries; always use parameterized queries ($1, $2).
- Ensure DB connections are handled via the `pool` in `src/db.js`.

## Port Management
- The server must always use `process.env.PORT || 3001`. Never hardcode `3000`.
